From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:02:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/36] calendar: index iCalendar attachments, query and send
 events

iCalendar files (`.ics` attachments and the `text/calendar` part of email
invitations, which mimeparser already turns into a File) are parsed once and
indexed in a `calendar_events` table, so a calendar UI can query a date
range without reading every blob, and reminders can later work natively.

- Parsing via the `icalendar` crate, recurrence via `rrule` (+ chrono-tz).
  One row per VEVENT; recurring series are stored as a serialized RRuleSet
  and expanded per query. TZIDs: IANA names, Mozilla-style path prefixes,
  a table of common Windows names (Outlook/Exchange), then the VTIMEZONE's
  fixed standard offset. All-day and floating times are wall-clock encoded
  as UTC and flagged, so the UI shows them unshifted.
- Updates: per (UID, RECURRENCE-ID) the highest SEQUENCE (then newest
  message) wins; METHOD:CANCEL / STATUS:CANCELLED mark it cancelled, and
  RECURRENCE-ID overrides replace the series occurrence they name.
- The table is derived data, created with CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS on
  open instead of a numbered migration (a fork migration number would
  collide with upstream's next one). Indexed on receive; messages from
  before, and attachments downloaded later, are indexed lazily on query.
  Housekeeping prunes entries of deleted messages.
- JSON-RPC: get_calendar_events(chat?, from, to), get_calendar_chats(),
  send_calendar_event(chat, event, text?) which writes the .ics and sends
  it as a File with the optional text.
